{
 "notes": ["PlusTech's CUSTOMIZE (original scene 26: setup 0x0302f3, the icons 0x0324bd, the list 0x03215c drawn by 0x0303d7, the level meter 0x031d63 drawn by 0x02f3fc, the question 0x031ae2, notices 0x031821). Opened from the PlusTech menu (data/ui/plustech.json), which EXIT goes back to.", "left/right move along the icons without wrapping (sys 3); confirm lists the player's parts of the icon's kind by name (0x0182b1), or says none; cancel jumps to EXIT (sys 4). In the list up/down choose, X and Y sort by name and price (sys 5), cancel goes back (sys 8) and confirm opens the meter.", "The meter chooses a level from levels[0] to levels[1] (left/right): below 0 LIGHT, 0 NORMAL, above 0 HEAVY. The price (0x02f37e) is the difference between the part's prices at the two levels, or, crossing level 0, the way down to level 0 and back up from it; red when the money will not do. confirm on a new level: poor, or the tune question (NO chosen); YES pays (sys 27) and sets the level. A fitted body left with fewer socket holes than its hangar's modules take has them all taken off (dismantled). cancel puts the level back.", "The stats panel shows the part at the level chosen; a part fitted in a hangar also shows the robot's TOTAL WEIGHT and its legs' WEIGHT CAPACITY with it (0x02f20f, 0x0baf8e). An arm or backpack weapon fitted shows which of the pair of slots holds it (0x017152): side_marks[0] for the hangar's first slot of the pair, [1] for the second.", "The part's 3D model the original turns in the details window (0x030228) is not drawn. The cancel hint's gap after the B button is the researcher's reading of 0x06ded3's last argument (0x13)."],
